{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 31, :comments ["<b>To put upon the turban above.</b> By means of the cords he would seat it upon the turban in the manner of a crown. And one cannot say the צִיץ was on the מִצְנֶפֶת, for behold, in the slaughter of consecrated offerings we learned: his hair was visible between the צִיץ and the מִצְנֶפֶת, there where he lays tefillin, and the צִיץ was placed on the forehead — behold, the מִצְנֶפֶת is above and the צִיץ below; so what is 'upon the מִצְנֶפֶת above'? And I further raised a difficulty on it: here it says ״וַיִּתְּנוּ עָלָיו פְּתִיל תְּכֵלֶת״, and in the matter of the command it says ״וְשַׂמְתָּ אוֹתוֹ עַל פְּתִיל תְּכֵלֶת״? And I say: this פְּתִיל תְּכֵלֶת is cords, to tie it with them to the מִצְנֶפֶת — because the צִיץ extends only from ear to ear, and with what would he tie it on his forehead? — and fixed in it were cords of תְּכֵלֶת at its two ends and at its middle, with which he ties it and suspends it on the מִצְנֶפֶת when it is on his head. And there were two cords at each and every end, one above and one below toward the forehead, and likewise at its middle — for thus it is easy to tie, and the manner of tying is not with fewer than two cords. Therefore it says 'upon a cord of תְּכֵלֶת,' and 'upon it a cord of תְּכֵלֶת.' And he ties their two heads all together behind him, opposite his neck, and seats it upon the מִצְנֶפֶת. And do not wonder that it does not say פְּתִילֵי תְּכֵלֶת since they are many, for behold, we find in the חֹשֶׁן and אֵפוֹד: ״וַיִּרְכְּסוּ אֶת הַחֹשֶׁן״ … ״בִּפְתִיל תְּכֵלֶת״, and perforce there were no fewer than two, for at the two ends of the חֹשֶׁן were two rings of the חֹשֶׁן, and at the two shoulder-pieces of the אֵפוֹד were two rings of the אֵפוֹד, opposite them, and by the manner of tying there were four cords — and in any case fewer than two is impossible."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:59.881142071Z", 